==================================================================================================
 DISCREPANCY READING (the bridge to hereditary discrepancy / arXiv:2607.00876)
==================================================================================================
 mean D_c = int_0^1 D_c(t) dt.  Independent (fully spread) heuristic for j arcs length 1/7:
 E[uncovered] = (1-1/7)^j (each of the 'gaps' empty w.p. ...) -- the AP is the LOW-discrepancy
 extreme (arcs sweep in lock-step => most simultaneous covering => smallest mean & smallest Q).
   independent-arcs reference (6/7)^7 = 0.339917
                      pattern  range   mean D_c   Q_c(3/7)  star-disc proxy
        (0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6)      6   0.297959   0.050688           0.1429
       (0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 12)     12   0.310664   0.077288           0.4405
      (0, 2, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12)     12   0.297958   0.050688           0.1429
     (0, 1, 3, 7, 15, 31, 63)     63   0.334200   0.100141           0.4762
    (0, 5, 9, 13, 17, 21, 25)     25   0.310831   0.074292           0.1429

 READING: AP (0..6) has the SMALLEST star-discrepancy of {c_i} AND the smallest floor Q_c -- the
 low-discrepancy/consecutive instance is the extremal (hardest) one, exactly as the DP counting
 lower bound is driven by the discrepancy of the prefix-sum (triangular) matrix. Spreading the c_i
 (higher range) RAISES the floor: the defect from the independent (6/7)^j reference shrinks with range.

