 (R2) VERDICT
==================================================================================================
  * F_7 minimized at the AP (range 6), value 0.050688 = 1.83 x 1/36; strictly increasing in range.
  * large-range spot checks (R up to 150): all >= AP floor and >= 1/36. Range > 14 is SAFER, not a gap.
  * j=8 same shape (AP argmin, all >= 1/36). The renormalization residual is pinned by the compact AP
    fixed point -- (R2)'s 'large-range patterns recurse/are safe' is confirmed: the min is at min range.
  * MECHANISM = discrepancy: the AP is the min-discrepancy (lock-step) config => max simultaneous
    covering => min density floor; higher range = higher discrepancy of {c_i} = larger floor.
  * STATUS: evidence-standard closure of (R2) (float grid T=6000, AP re-validated vs S33 exact). The
    remaining proof step is Schur-convexity of Q_c in the gap-vector (AP = all-gaps-equal = the
    rearrangement minimizer) -- shaped, not open-ended.
DONE.
